/-!
# Structurality from `Equation3727` through the companion `x □ y = ((x ◇ y) ◇ (x ◇ x))`

Generated by `defwork/wffit.py`.  `Equation3727` is `x ◇ y = (x ◇ y) ◇ (z ◇ x)`.  The source half is
`AutBox.WordRigidFull`: two finite models of `Equation3727` on one carrier with the same table of
`((x ◇ y) ◇ (x ◇ x))` are the same model.  That is what makes the companion's automorphisms automorphisms of
`◇`, and it mentions no map, so `grind` can do it.  Each theorem below then only has to check that
the source forces its target of the companion.
-/

open FirstOrder FirstOrder.Language Law Law.MagmaLaw FreeMagma

set_option maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option linter.unusedSimpArgs false
